WEBVTT

00:02:58.556 --> 00:03:01.276
are what is called "social
evaluative threat" --

00:03:01.276 --> 00:03:04.276
threats to self-esteem or social status,

00:03:04.276 --> 00:03:07.316
where others can negatively
judge your performance.

00:03:07.796 --> 00:03:11.836
So although these social stresses
are widely recognized

00:03:11.876 --> 00:03:13.516
and we're all familiar with them,

00:03:14.356 --> 00:03:18.956
people fail to see how inequality
makes them worse for all of us.

00:03:19.596 --> 00:03:21.156
In this slide,

00:03:21.156 --> 00:03:24.556
along the bottom, you've got
different income groups,

00:03:24.596 --> 00:03:27.156
from the poorest tenth
of the population on the left

00:03:27.156 --> 00:03:28.796
to the richest on the right.

00:03:28.836 --> 00:03:30.476
And up the side,